---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ContactSupportSection from '../../components/ContactSupportSection.astro';
import { getPageSeoEntry } from '../../config/pageSeo';
import { breadcrumbSchema, webPageSchema } from '../../utils/schema';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const seo = getPageSeoEntry('/contact/')!;
const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Contact', path: '/contact/' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={seo.title}
  description={seo.description}
  logoAlt="Contact – site logo"
  jsonLd={[
    webPageSchema({ name: seo.title, description: seo.description, url: '/contact/' }),
    breadcrumbSchema(breadcrumbs),
  ]}
>
  <section class="border-b border-border bg-muted/20 py-8 md:py-10">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5">
      <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs} />
    </div>
  </section>
  <ContactSupportSection titleId="contact-page-title" showTicketTips />

  <article class="content-markdown contact-page-shell border-t border-border bg-muted/10 py-10 md:py-12">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5">
      <h2>When to use this contact page</h2>
      <p>
        Reach out when you need help interpreting plan previews, screenshots, or affiliate checkout steps on arc-cheats.net—not when you already have a vendor ticket open for the same order.
      </p>
      <p>
        We answer questions about how guides map to modules, which stills prove a feature, and whether an add-on requires extra hardware. License delivery and payment disputes stay with the vendor named on your receipt.
      </p>
      <h2>What we can help with</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Clarifying homepage pricing previews versus final checkout totals</li>
        <li>Pointing you to the right guide: ESP, aim, requirements, DMA, or ban risk</li>
        <li>Explaining how affiliate links attribute sales without changing list price</li>
        <li>Reporting broken links or outdated screenshots on this domain</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What we cannot do</h2>
      <p>
        We do not reset HWIDs, issue refunds, or toggle ban status. We do not distribute loaders or binaries through email.
        We cannot see your vendor dashboard; only their support team can resend keys or extend subscriptions.
      </p>
      <h2>Proof and offers referenced on-site</h2>
      <p>
        Module pages include dated stills—skeleton ESP, loot filters, indoor breach lighting, and menu tabs. Those images are editorial evidence, not live telemetry from your PC.
      </p>
      <p>
        Offers shown in copy mirror the hero at the time of publishing: <strong>$35</strong> monthly and <strong>$150</strong> lifetime for the standard bundle unless a banner states otherwise. Confirm every promotion on the vendor cart before you pay.
      </p>
      <h2>Before you write</h2>
      <p>
        Read the <a href="/faq/">checkout and DMA FAQ</a>, the <a href="/guides/system-requirements/">PC requirements guide</a>, and the feature article that matches your question
        (<a href="/arc-raiders-esp/">loot and player markers</a> or <a href="/arc-raiders-aimbot/">aimbot field notes</a>).
        Tickets with screenshots and Windows build numbers get faster answers than one-line “it broke” messages.
      </p>
      <h2>Typical reply windows</h2>
      <p>
        Messages about outdated screenshots or unclear plan language usually get a same-week reply. We route billing questions back to your vendor when the receipt already shows an open ticket ID.
      </p>
      <p>
        Include your timezone if you need a call-style walkthrough; most answers stay async with links to the right guide so you can bookmark steps.
      </p>
      <h2>Enforcement and risk email</h2>
      <p>
        We cannot remove flags or speak for Embark support. Point enforcement questions to the
        <a href="/arc-raiders-account-vs-hardware-ban/">account strike versus HWID explainer</a> first, then your game account portal.
      </p>
      <h2>DMA and optional add-ons</h2>
      <p>
        When your message mentions passthrough firmware, attach output from the
        <a href="/guides/cloud-dma-setup/">passthrough DMA prep walkthrough</a> and note whether standard ESP worked before you enabled hypervisor steps.
      </p>
      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Support email may log your address and message body to respond. We do not sell contact lists. Details appear in the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy for analytics and email</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        For commission transparency, see the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">partner commission statement</a> before you follow a checkout bridge.
      </p>
      <h2>Editorial corrections</h2>
      <p>
        Report typos, wrong plan figures, or mismatched stills with the page URL in the first line. We prioritize corrections on money URLs (
        <a href="/arc-raiders-esp/">loot marker coverage</a>,
        <a href="/">homepage plan hero</a>) before forum placeholders.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>